{"commit": "2428c152a67c06057a98d9d29b08389cb3429c1f", "id": "2428c152a67c06057a98d9d29b08389cb3429c1f-1", "language": "rust", "reason": "Proposal names no upstream test", "repo": "https://github.com/tokio-rs/bytes", "reproduction": {"attempt": "20260923T230154Z-3d15e4e5", "evidence_sha256": {"evidence/2428c152a67c06057a98d9d29b08389cb3429c1f-1/20260923T230154Z-3d15e4e5/origin.json": "e673178025782fa396f21ae669d781148c1bcd1e539b2d55313287cc8f3f8a3d", "evidence/2428c152a67c06057a98d9d29b08389cb3429c1f-1/20260923T230154Z-3d15e4e5/proposal.json": "f35988b07bf75b2d5fcf539462e79efaa269c7ceb9f7017733daf322f37533c3"}, "provenance": "verbatim"}, "shard": "bytes", "status": "blocked", "subject": "Panic on integer overflow in Chain::remaining (#482)", "summary": "`Chain::remaining` summed the halves with a wrapping `+`, so when the combined length exceeded `usize::MAX` it silently underflowed to a smaller value. The fix switches to `saturating_add`, preserving a lower bound of `max(a, b)`.", "updated_at": "2026-09-23T23:01:54.998544+00:00"}
